{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>There shall no longer be…</b> The subject of this passage is that those who return to Zion in the days of the Messiah will live many years, and the old man will fill his days according to the natural lifespan, like the ancients from Adam to Noah; likewise עול ימים, which is the infant. And the one who dies—dies when he is a hundred years old, and if he dies he is cursed, for if he lives fewer than these years, they will say of him: his mind is not yet fully formed. This is the meaning of 'dies while still a youth,' and the sinner, if he reaches a hundred. Scripture testifies that the end of the world will return to its beginning."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 65, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:01:06.447256287Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}